# The runtime is a pinned governance fact, not a floor. `engines.node` in
# package.json names the exact version in .nvmrc, and engine-strict makes pnpm
# REFUSE to install on anything else instead of warning.
#
# Why exact: this repo's local tooling is not portable across Node majors. The
# local-stack orchestrator (scripts/local-stack/stack.ts) drives docker compose
# through spawnSync, and on Node 26 that fails `ENOBUFS` mid-boot — after the
# containers are up, with a diagnostics collector that then fails the same way,
# so the symptom looks like a broken stack rather than a wrong runtime. The
# fenced AI-language suites are stricter still: their group tables are generated
# from ICU 78.2 / Unicode 17.0, which is exactly what 22.23.2 ships
# (scripts/check-test-quality.mjs PINNED_RUNTIME).
engine-strict=true
